// DF-232f, the REFUSAL: the entry file is OUTSIDE the mapped package, so a
// `public(package)` symbol of that package is not its to name. Before the fix
// this compiled and ran — `check_visibility` fails OPEN when no package root
// is known (namespace.py, the `if not package_root: return True` arm), and
// nothing ever set a root for a --module-path module — so the tier silently
// degraded to `public` for exactly the packages that most wanted it.
//
// `secret_is_reachable` next to it is genuinely `public`, so this refusal is
// about the TIER, not about `pkgvis.secret` being unreachable.
// The refusal lands AT THE IMPORT, names the tier and the defining module,
// and its hint offers both the fix and what this module does export — so
// asserting the shape, not just the symbol, is what keeps a future
// regression from passing this pin with a vaguer message.
// EXPECT: error
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: `pkg_secret` is public(package) in `pkgvis.secret`
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: mark it `public` in `pkgvis.secret` to expose it
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: available: secret_is_reachable
// COMPILE-FLAGS: --module-path pkgvis={TESTDIR}/modules/pkgvis232f
import pkgvis.secret.{pkg_secret, secret_is_reachable}

func main() {
    print(pkg_secret() + secret_is_reachable())
}
